      "content": "Here's a revised draft:\n\nSubject: Update on Senior DevOps Engineer Role\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Senior DevOps Engineer role at [Company Name]. We appreciate the time and effort you invested in our interview process, and we're grateful for the opportunity to have learned more about your skills and experience. Your enthusiasm for cloud security and Kubernetes was particularly impressive, and we were struck by your ability to think creatively about scaling microservices - a trait that's not always easy to find, even among seasoned engineers.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we've decided to move forward with another candidate whose background in scaling microservices for high-traffic environments aligns more closely with our current needs. Please know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were impressed by your technical skills, particularly in Kubernetes and cloud security.\n\nI want to assure you that this decision is in no way a reflection on your abilities or potential as a DevOps engineer. Your passion for cloud security and Kubernetes is evident, and we have no doubt that you'll excel in a role that aligns with your strengths.\n\nAlthough we won't be moving forward with you at this time, we'd like to keep your",
